__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.stamp

# hand-off bundles built from shares; the repo publishes files, not archives
*.zip

# superseded draft material kept on disk for traceability, not for publishing
# (may contain local/machine-specific paths — see the archive's own README)
skill-toolkit/skills/scientific-research-guide/archive/
/archive/
*.lock

# `.claude/` stays ignored on `main`: ADOPTERS.md promises this repo is reference
# material, not a live config, and a tracked `.claude/` would install itself into
# anyone who opens the clone as a workspace. The three negations below exist ONLY
# on the `claude/cloud-env-*` branch, which is never merged — see .claude/README.md.
.claude/*
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/README.md
!.claude/sync-from-repo.sh
